      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Joins up to eight video clips into one video, WITH their sound: cut the start or end of each clip, pick how they meet, fade in and out, loop, or lay one song under the whole video. No model: it runs in seconds.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The demo: four clips of the SAME 10 seconds of the same man talking. The original, and his new looks from workflow <b>07</b> (VFX Edit), <b>08</b> (outfit from pictures) and <b>02</b> (Character Swap). Each clip shows the NEXT 2.5 seconds of his sentence, so he keeps talking while his look changes.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"to-do\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Steps</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li><b>1.</b> to <b>4.</b> Load your clips in the order they should play, one <b>Load Video</b> each.</li><li><b>5.</b> On <b>Video Tools</b>, set the cuts, the join and the fades (see below). The timeline on the node follows every change.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b>. <b>Play</b> on Video Tools shows a small moving preview, the saved video plays on <b>Save Video</b>.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"video\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;How the demo is set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>clip 1: <b>Cut start 0</b>, <b>Cut end 180</b>. It keeps the first 2.5 seconds.</li><li>clip 2: <b>Cut start 52</b>, <b>Cut end 123</b>.</li><li>clip 3: <b>Cut start 112</b>, <b>Cut end 63</b>.</li><li>clip 4: <b>Cut start 172</b>, <b>Cut end 3</b>.</li><li><b>Join: Crossfade</b>, Length <b>8</b> frames. A crossfade lays the last 8 frames of one clip over the first 8 of the next. Each clip here starts 8 frames BEFORE the one before it stops, so during the crossfade both show the same moment with the same sound: his voice runs on with no jump while one look melts into the next.</li><li><b>Fade In 6</b>, <b>Out 12</b> frames: up from black at the start, down to black at the end. The sound fades with it.</li><li>Cuts count in <b>frames</b>: at 24 frames a second, 24 frames = 1 second, 60 = 2.5 seconds.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;With your own clips</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>More clips:</b> each time you wire a clip, a new free pair of inputs (<b>video</b> + <b>audio</b>) appears, up to eight.</li><li><b>Join:</b> <b>Cut</b> = one right after the other, <b>Crossfade</b> = one melts into the next, <b>Through black</b> = a short dip to black between them.</li><li><b>Match colors</b> helps when one clip continues another (a clip made from the last frame of the one before) and comes out a little darker or warmer.</li><li><b>A music video:</b> load a song with <b>Load Audio Pixaroma</b> and drop its wire on the <b>music</b> dot of Video Tools. <b>Only music</b> leaves the clips' own sound out, <b>Music + clip sound</b> keeps both. The song is cut to the video's length and fades with it.</li><li><b>Loop:</b> <b>Repeat</b> plays it again, <b>Ping-pong</b> goes forward then backwards, <b>Seamless</b> blends the end into the start for a video that loops with no jump.</li><li><b>&#10226; Back</b> on a clip plays it backwards, its sound too.</li><li>Every clip takes the size of clip 1 (the gear sets Fill, Fit or Stretch). Keep one frame rate for all clips: the Load Video nodes here all load at 24.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
