      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Video Pixaroma (1. clip 1, the original)</b> - Clip 1, the original video. Every clip is loaded at <b>480 x 864</b>, the size the H3 clips were made at, so they all match.</li><li><b>Load Video Pixaroma (2. clip 2, workflow 07)</b> - Clip 2: the same video after workflow 07. It follows the original frame for frame and carries the original sound.</li><li><b>Load Video Pixaroma (3. clip 3, workflow 08)</b> - Clip 3: the same video after workflow 08. It follows the original frame for frame and carries the original sound.</li><li><b>Load Video Pixaroma (4. clip 4, workflow 02)</b> - Clip 4: the same video after workflow 02. It follows the original frame for frame and carries the original sound.</li><li><b>Video Tools Pixaroma (5. how to join them)</b> - Joins the clips in order, with their sound. Each clip is cut to its own 2.5 seconds of the sentence (<b>Cut start</b> / <b>Cut end</b>), the joins are <b>Crossfades</b> of 8 frames, and the video fades in and out at the ends. The timeline on the node shows it all.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Video Pixaroma (the joined video)</b> - Saves the joined video as MP4 into <code>ComfyUI/output/Joined Videos</code> and plays it on the node.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Video Pixaroma (1. clip 1, the original)</b> - Clip 1, the original video. Every clip is loaded at <b>480 x 864</b>, the size the H3 clips were made at, so they all match.</li><li><b>Load Video Pixaroma (2. clip 2, workflow 07)</b> - Clip 2: the same video after workflow 07. It follows the original frame for frame and carries the original sound.</li><li><b>Load Video Pixaroma (3. clip 3, workflow 08)</b> - Clip 3: the same video after workflow 08. It follows the original frame for frame and carries the original sound.</li><li><b>Load Video Pixaroma (4. clip 4, workflow 02)</b> - Clip 4: the same video after workflow 02. It follows the original frame for frame and carries the original sound.</li><li><b>Video Tools Pixaroma (5. how to join them)</b> - Joins the clips in order, with their sound. Each clip is cut to its own 2.5 seconds of the sentence (<b>Cut start</b> / <b>Cut end</b>), the joins are <b>Crossfades</b> of 8 frames, and the video fades in and out at the ends. The timeline on the node shows it all.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Video Pixaroma (the joined video)</b> - Saves the joined video as MP4 into <code>ComfyUI/output/Joined Videos</code> and plays it on the node.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      },
